{"type":"text","timestamp":1794590126566,"sessionID":"ses_e2a1b2d6effeZWID03PyQ7ZVJd","part":{"id":"prt_1d5e82488001y6uz9gqFH2UTOY","sessionID":"ses_e2a1b2d6effeZWID03PyQ7ZVJd","messageID":"msg_1d5e8144c001hSTX7q39sMiR9z","type":"text","text":"T008 is complete.\n\n## Files written\n\n1. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`\n   - Added `readFileSync` (`node:fs`) and `join` (`node:path`) imports.\n   - Added `it('the command-bridges README names every command row field')` inside `describe('generated command table')`. It reads `lib/command-attach.ts` and `scripts/command-bridges/README.md`, extracts the `CommandRow` fields with `/readonly (\\w+)\\??:/g`, asserts `['command', 'policy', 'mutating', 'ownerSkillId']`, then asserts the `Each row carries` sentence names each field in backticks.\n\n2. `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`\n   - Replaced the old `Each row carries …` sentence with the four named fields.\n\n## Verify output\n\nTest-first run (before the README edit) failed on the first name, as the task predicted:\n\n```\n × the command-bridges README names every command row field\nAssertionError: expected 'Each row carries the runnable slash c…' to contain '`command`'\nExpected: \"`command`\"\nReceived: \"Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. …\"\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 20 passed (21)\n```\n\nAfter the README edit:\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed (21)\n```\n\n`rg -c \"its derived policy and the owning skill\" $CBR` printed nothing and exited 1, which is the expected no-match.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The diff for `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` also shows T003's concurrent changes in `CAG` (`isNoEditRequest`, `NOEDIT4`). Those were already on disk from another worker when I read the file. I left them untouched.\n- I did not tick the checkbox in `tasks.md`.\n- I did not run the packet-wide spec validation or the full suite, since neither is this task's named gate and other lanes are mid-flight.","time":{"start":1794590123144,"end":1794590126566}}}
